{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לשבעת הימים", :translit "l'shivat ha-yamim", :gloss "for the seven days"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "לשבעת הימים", :b "לימי אבל מתושלח"}], :frame {:text "Methuselah died shortly before the Flood, and the seven days before the deluge (Genesis 7:10) correspond to the seven days of mourning (shiv'ah) for him. The practice of seven days of mourning traces to the mourning of Joseph over Jacob: Genesis 50:10 records that Joseph observed a seven-day mourning period, and the Talmud establishes this as the model for the rabbinic enactment of shiv'ah (Sanhedrin 20a; Mo'ed Katan 20a).", :sources ["Genesis 50:10" "Sanhedrin 20a" "Mo'ed Katan 20a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "לשבעת הימים", :a-value 907, :b "לימי אבל מתושלח", :b-value 907, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:04:44.516128635Z", :model "glm-5.2"}